# Copy to .env.local and adjust for your environment. Never commit real values.

# Base URL of the backend API (apps/api). No trailing slash. Never hard-code the Render
# deployment URL — remote environments configure this via their own env var mechanism
# (Vercel/Render/etc. project settings), the same way apps/api's DATABASE_URL/R2 credentials
# are configured (see docs/DEPLOYMENT_FREE.md).
#
# Local dev note: `npm run web:dev` runs this app on port 3001 (apps/api/main.ts defaults to
# 3000) specifically so both can run side by side without colliding. For the httpOnly
# refresh-token cookie / CORS credentials flow to work against a locally-running backend, its
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS must include this app's exact origin (http://localhost:3001) — see
# docs/frontend/FRONTEND_AUTH.md "Local development: CORS".
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
